@startuml codex-renewal
!theme plain
title Codex personal plan: one auth owner refreshes; launches use external tokens and renew without a restart

participant "Codex app-server\n(agent OS user, no auth.json)" as A
participant "Launcher\n(client of the app-server)" as L
participant "Broker: auth owner\n(holds auth.json + lock)" as O

L -> O: lease.request {harness: codex_cli, channel: external-token, …}
O -> O: token expires within 48 h? refresh once (one-shot codex app-server)
O --> L: {access_token, chatgpt_account_id, expires_at}
L -> A: initialize; account/login/start {type: chatgptAuthTokens, accessToken, chatgptAccountId}
... turns ...
A -> A: model call answers 401
A -> L: account/chatgptAuthTokens/refresh
L -> O: lease.renew {lease_id, rejected_sha256}
alt rejected token is still current
  O -> O: refresh once under the lock (N rejected launches → 1 refresh)
end
O --> L: new access token
L --> A: refresh answer {accessToken}
A -> A: retry; the turn continues (no restart)
note over O: the refresh token never leaves the auth owner
@enduml
